{
  "about": "Vectors of the whole-value pattern rule. connectors-catalog has the rule (inventory::pattern_matches) and connectors-host has a copy of it for standing grants (local::standing). A test in each crate reads this file: local::standing::tests::the_shared_pattern_vectors_hold and whole_value_patterns::the_shared_pattern_vectors_hold. `matches` is null where the rule refuses the pattern itself. No vector depends on a compiled-size limit: the two crates set different ones. The host's rule refuses two more things, and no vector holds either: a pattern that turns case-insensitive matching on while Unicode matching is on (`(?i)`, `(?i:...)`, or `(?u)` under a fold), which the catalog's rule takes, and a value longer than the pattern's `max_value_bytes`, which the host does not match. So every fold in these vectors is written with Unicode matching off; the vectors on `^(?-u)s|(?i)k$`, `^(?i-u:s)(?s:k)$` and `^(?-u:(?i)s)(?u)k$` tell whether a flag holds over a `|` and whether a fold ends with the group that set it.",
